{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/shuffled()"},"abstract":[{"text":"Inherited from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence.shuffled()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Cliques","relatedModules":["Swift"]}],"symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:STsE8shuffledSay7ElementQzGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","extendedModule":"Swift","title":"shuffled()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shuffled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shuffled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/shuffled()"]}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","title":"MaximalCliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","title":"Cliques","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/shuffled()":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/shuffled()","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/shuffled()","title":"shuffled()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shuffled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]}}}